# OpenClaw Virtuozzo Package

Single-file JPS install manifest for OpenClaw on Virtuozzo (formerly Jelastic branding in docs/tests).

## Repo layout

- `manifest.jps` — install package (source of truth)
- `addons/configure-ai-models.jps` — standalone copy of configure-ai-models addon (type: update)
- `addons/update-openclaw-latest.jps` — standalone copy of update-openclaw-latest addon (type: update)
- `scripts/configureModelsOnBeforeInit.js` — addon UI: query current models from container
- `tests/smoke-test.sh` — smoke tests on cp node
- `tests/test-cases.md` — manual/auto test matrix
- `../.cursor/rules/openclaw-manifest.mdc` — parent `sych/` rule (keep in sync)

## Install scope (manifest.jps)

**On install:** gateway only — no AI model configuration.

- Docker-in-Docker on cp node (`jelastic/docker-ce:latest`)
- Container `openclaw`, state at `/data/openclaw`, port 80→18789
- Dynamic credentials: `oc_${fn.uuid}`, `pw_${fn.password}`
- `start.sh`: npm install openclaw, gateway token auth, bind lan, trustedProxies, device auto-approval, `gateway run`
- Do **not** add `openclaw models set` or `onboard` to install unless explicitly requested

**After install:** user configures models via Add-ons → Configure AI Models, or manually with `openclaw onboard` inside the container.

## Model configuration rules

- Never use bare `openclaw models set` without prior `openclaw onboard --non-interactive` (causes Unknown model errors)
- Do not use deprecated `google/gemini-2.5-flash`; prefer `google/gemini-3-flash-preview`
- After onboard, restore Virtuozzo gateway settings: token auth, bind lan, trustedProxies
- Top providers for configure-ai-models addon: OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini
- `google`/`openai`/`openrouter` may not appear in `models list --all` until auth is configured; use `plugins list` for provider IDs

## Addons

**Current:** `configure-ai-models`, `update-openclaw-latest`.

**configure-ai-models:** optional API keys for OpenAI / Anthropic / Gemini; `onBeforeInit` runs `openclaw models list` and `models status --json` in the container to populate the default model dropdown and show current state. Uses `openclaw onboard --non-interactive` before `models set`; restores Virtuozzo gateway settings after onboard.

## Branding

- User-facing text: **Virtuozzo** (not Jelastic)
- Keep `jelastic/docker-ce:latest` image name — technical Docker Hub reference

